    affiliation: "DIGIP, University of Bergamo"
keywords:
  - crates.io
  - Rust
  - package abandonment
  - software ecosystems
  - survival analysis
  - mining software repositories
abstract: >-
  Point-in-time feature tables for every mature crates.io package at yearly
  cutoffs 2019-2024 plus a 2026 snapshot, GitHub maintainer-activity signals
  reconstructed as of each cutoff, outcome labels derived from RustSec
  advisories and repository archival, a 300-crate human/LLM-adjudicated gold
  set, and the pipeline that builds them and trains the calibrated
  abandonment-forecasting model shipped in cargo-pulse.
related:
  - type: software
    title: cargo-pulse
    url: https://crates.io/crates/cargo-pulse
